There's more levels below Mines Town. Mines End has
some special stuff, both to help you and to hurt
you. It doesn't sound like you have them yet.

 > My next question is, is sokoban really necessary?
 > Already having a BoH, and SDSM....is it?

Partially that depends on how you feel about pushing
rocks and solving puzzles. It has some guaranteed
wands and food and rings. There's a fair amount of
money at the end beyond the prize. Probably the most
unnoticed benefit is on strength: pushing all those
boulders for all that time exercises strength, and
strength is something you can use.

On the other hand, it is _astonishingly_ easy to
starve to death in Sokoban in the midst of all that
food, just from being distracted. Each level takes
_lots_ of turns, and you need to alternate eating
and praying for food, if you want to have any hope
of exiting with a food surplus.

